<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan CPC tenders to buy July fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC tenders to buy July fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy two 0.5-percent sulphur fuel oil cargoes for July deliveries, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>CPC seeks to buy the low-pour cargo for July 16-30 delivery and the high-pour cargo for July 1-30 to Keelung, Taichung or Shenao on a cost-and-freight basis (c-and-f) basis, the official said.</p>
<p>The tender will close on June 4 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last fuel oil purchase, CPC bought two 38,000-tonne cargoes of 0.5-percent fuel oil at around $124 per tonne for July 1-10 delivery.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65 8703571)</p>
